Package: com.example.multifloat
Name: MultiFloat
Version: 0.17.0
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: Multi-floating window / split-view tweak for iOS 17 (roothide / arm64e). 0.17.0 fixes the regression that made switching flash MORE often and turned the flash white. Archive 17 pins two causes. First, the tiered real-black recovery escalated per tick (L1 at tick 1, L2 at tick 2, L3 at tick 3), but a level-1 write recovers asynchronously: the scene resubmission takes 400 to 800 ms to show up as layers. So a healthy level-1 write was misread as ineffective, the next tick escalated to a frame write and the one after to a displayConfiguration write, producing 27 geometry writes in one session (16 L2 + 11 L3, versus a single L2 in the previous archive); every one of them reasserts presenter geometry or flips the display configuration, which is exactly the white-flash-then-content the user reports. 0.17.0 adds a take-effect confirmation window: after writing tier N the watchdog keeps writing tier N for at least two more ticks before escalating, and the escalation thresholds move from 2/3 to 3/5 ticks. Second, the preventive-tier foreground keep-alive (added in 0.15.0) was proven useless across three archives: because FBScene.foreground is unreadable on this device, every preventive episode wrote at least one frame (37 preventive writes, zero no-delta results), while the real-black count never dropped (92, then 93). Each updateSettingsWithBlock costs one full scene resubmission = one visible flash frame, so the keep-alive was pure cost. keepAlivePreventForeground now defaults to NO (one-time migration; the life-saving setForeground:YES inside the real-black L1 write is untouched, so the 0.13.0 black-screen fix is not affected). Also per user request, hostEnabled now defaults to YES so the floating window works without a config edit before first use. Config version migrates 17 to 18.
Maintainer: QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Author: QingC12
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 15.0)
